      "realworld_contexts": [
        {
          "context": "ICL data-poisoning defense with a semantic trigger: a trigger phrase planted in poisoned few-shot demonstrations flips the label the model copies for triggered test inputs (Kandpal et al. 2023-style ICL backdoor / Wan et al. 2023 instruction poisoning). Cut the (trigger-content query × poisoned-label key) cells so triggered inputs classify normally, while untriggered few-shot classification and the trigger phrase's ordinary meaning are untouched.",
          "mechanism": "Label emission at the test position is carried by label-copying/induction heads attending back to demonstration labels — the proven in-context-backdoor structure. With a planted trigger, the query-side match feature IS the trigger content (distinctive, rare-in-legit-text phrase features at the test input), and the key is the poisoned-label token (common — every untriggered demo legitimately reuses the same label tokens). The conjunction (trigger-query × flipped-label-key) fires only on the attack: textbook clause-4 with a content query.",
          "why_linear_steer_fails": "A content-gated steer must suppress either the trigger direction (corrupting the phrase's ordinary semantics wherever it appears) or the label direction (breaking ALL ICL classification, since clean demos use the same label tokens); even gated to attack positions, the residual write is read by every head's Q/K/V and the MLP there. FRA cuts only the pairing — clean demos fail the conjunction.",
          "model_benchmark": "gemma-2-2b + Kandpal et al. 2023-style poisoned SST-2/AG-News few-shot suites (metrics: attack success rate + clean ICL accuracy), GemmaScope res 65k; gpt2-small fallback with token-label copy streams (res-jb).",
