          "mechanism": "L10H7's QK is a per-token FAMILY of separable cells: (about-to-predict-X query) × (X-appeared-earlier key). The query content is target-specific by construction (the one X), so the conjunction never recurs for other tokens; the key endpoint (X in context) is common — exactly the high-A regime of the magnitude law. CCF 0.98 and LBNR R=+0.95 already measured.",
          "why_linear_steer_fails": "Projection-removal of the X-direction (either endpoint) destroys X's representation in every prompt where X appears — the measured 26,000×-class collateral signature; head-ablation releases suppression for ALL tokens at once (measured 0.503 vs FRA 0.022 collateral). Only the cell edit releases one token's suppression and transfers across contexts.",
          "model_benchmark": "gpt2-small + the copy-suppression paper's OWT/CSPA eval distribution (McDougall et al. 2023), res-jb SAEs; primary metric = legit-content KL vs the content-gated projection-removal steer at matched release.",
