          "mechanism": "Verbatim continuation of in-context text is induction over the passage's own tokens: (query = current passage token — distinctive content per passage) × (key = successor token at the earlier occurrence). Cutting the passage-specific cell set severs only the copy CHANNEL through induction heads; the passage content still enters the residual stream at its own positions and remains readable by every other edge/head/MLP — which is precisely what no residual-space intervention can arrange.",
          "why_linear_steer_fails": "Any steer that suppresses the passage tokens' directions to stop copying also removes that content from ALL readers — QA and paraphrase die with the copying (the broadcast problem). A position-patch blocks one location but not the content-addressed recurrence. FRA is the only intervention whose effect is channel-specific (one head-family's softmax) rather than content-destroying.",
          "model_benchmark": "gpt2-small for the copy-block arm (verbatim-overlap / longest-common-subsequence copy-rate on planted passages, res-jb); gemma-2-2b + GemmaScope 65k for the QA-preservation arm (cloze/QA accuracy about the passage at matched copy suppression).",
