        {
          "context": "Poisoned-context retrieval / RAG-style indirect prompt injection (PoisonedRAG, Zou et al. 2024, scaled down): the model answers a question from a poisoned passage in context; cut the (question-content query × poison-answer key) cells so the poisoned answer is not retrieved, while the poison string's ordinary meaning, the legitimate passages' edges, and answers to other questions survive. Cycle-1 deferred this on weak base elicitation (gemma-base P=0.027), NOT on principle — rerun with few-shot QA scaffolding to raise base P before screening.",
