      "notes": "CONSOLIDATION: 21 brainstormed entries deduped to 20 distinct candidates. Three copy-suppression-RELEASE entries (rank-3 'most de-risked', the L10H7+L11H10-union corpus entry, and the 'misfire-repair' sign-variant) all target the SAME head-family/mechanism/eval-distribution and are merged into ranked #1. Two occupational-gender-pronoun entries merged into #9. The in-context-coreference-backdoor (#8) and natural-Winograd-coreference (#17, LOSE) are kept distinct (planted-trigger content-query vs generic-role-query — the clause-4 discriminator). Gemma-knowledge-conflict (#15) is kept as the measured-LOSE paired contrast to gpt2 Ortu (#5).\n\nRANKING ANCHORED ON MEASURED IN-REPO RESULTS (experiments/fra_win/CAMPAIGN_REPORT.md + multitrigger_sleeper/summary.md). CONFIRMED WINS: retrieval two-needle ~1100x, acronym ~26,000x, induction ~15x/235x, in-context-backdoor flip (FRA 0.07 vs DoM 1.83/conv-SAE 6.06), copy-suppression s3 single-prompt (R=+0.95, FRA 0.022 vs head-ablate 0.503, A=22.7x). CONFIRMED LOSSES: docstring R=0.08, delimiter CCF 0.732/R=0.23, shared-endpoint box A=1.9x->7.9x, entity-PII differential NO-OP at strong base, knowledge-conflict gemma R=0.24, many-shot jailbreak (direction-routed), weight-baked sleeper (output-direction, DoM wins), fact-recall (base P too weak + MLP). The multitrigger sprint adds a HARD lesson directly relevant here: even for a clean in-context backdoor, FRA's value was diagnostic/selectional/localizing, NOT a better steering direction, and detector-feature != payload — but the QK CELL EDIT (not OV ablation) is the load-bearing win, which the shortlist all target.\n\nKEY PREDICTOR APPLICATION (FRA wins iff CCF-high AND LBNR-high; unique value = separability vs a content-gated linear steer):\n- The 5 shortlisted all have (a) a genuine content x content conjunction with a DISTINCTIVE-CONTENT discriminating endpoint (clause-4 satisfied: copy-supp query=about-to-predict-T; ICL query=trigger-phrase; NIAH query=queried-key-string; class-union key=digit-class with content attribute-query; Ortu query=fact-frame, key=counterfactual attribute), (b) direct OV-consumption (the attended/written content IS the behavior), and (c) a real reuse gap so a content-gated steer collaterals.\n- WHERE MOST CANDIDATES DIE (heaviest weight): redundancy/distributed/direction-routed/MLP. Killed or down-ranked on this: repetition-loop (#6, MLP repetition neurons + logit self-reinforcement + R-fold edge redundancy), gemma-gender (#9, synergistic multi-head + possible output-direction), alias-jailbreak (#10, MLP re-derivation + binding-adjacency), relation-selective recall (#11, shared-endpoint -> measured 1.9x floor prior), Dyck (#12, depth-role query + counter-MLP), gemma copy-supp (#13, published evidence of distributed/no-clean-unembedding + REACH ceiling), anti-induction (#14, net-cancellation LBNR + synthetic-only), and the four hard LOSES (#16 agreement = MLP morphology + redundancy; #17 Winograd = generic-role + distributed binding; #19 parametric recall = ~150 heads additive + MLP; #20 IOI duplicate = self-repair + pointer-not-OV).\n\nREACH vs SEPARABILITY caveat threaded throughout: the gemma soft-cap + SAE granularity (65k sweet spot, 1M fragments at fixed K) + GPT-2 LN-centering bound REMOVAL COMPLETENESS, not the separability verdict — they can make a matched-removal operating point hard to hit (the candidate-13 risk) but never flip a win to a lose once that point exists.\n\nFEASIBILITY NOW: all 5 shortlisted reuse existing harness code (s3_copysupp_tier2.py, ic*.py, r2_fra_retrieval.py, g5_s2gemma.py differential cells, acronym_steer3.py / retrieval_steer3.py projection-removal baseline, g_screen.py CCF, s2_lbnr.py). #1 and #5 are gpt2-small (cheapest, res-jb SAEs already loaded); #2/#3/#4 are gemma-2-2b + GemmaScope 65k (RMSNorm-exact FRA correction). Each fits one RunPod GPU tranche. Per user MEMORY: run on RunPod not local; rank heads by CAUSAL edge-cut not raw attention (raw attention picks sink/positional heads); standard fair baseline = content-gated PROJECTION-REMOVAL steer (not SAE-feature-subtraction, which nan'd on gemma / didn't fire on gpt2) compared on legit-content KL at MATCHED on-target removal; train/eval split (extraction/selection disjoint from eval).\n\nTOP RECOMMENDATION: spend GPU first on #1 (copy-suppression corpus, lowest-lift highest-confidence, a true external-validity upgrade of a measured win) and #2 (ICL-poisoning, highest safety importance, published benchmark, same mechanism as a measured win), then #3 (NIAH, best published LBNR evidence) — #4 and #5 are higher-variance (synthetic-prerequisite / scale-dilution-re-measure respectively) but high-value if the first three land."
